WEBVTT

NOTE The Immigrant (1917) - Riah TV captions

00:00:01.250 --> 00:00:08.240
Charles Chaplin
in "The Immigrant"

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:14.990
Cast: Immigrants, Charlie
Chaplin and Edna Purviance.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:21.240
The Head Waiter, Eric Campbell.
A Diner, Albert Austin. The
Artist, Henry Bergman.

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:26.250
Photographed by R. H. Totheroh.
Written and directed by Charles
Chaplin.

00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:30.450
[music]

00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:11.000
Dinner time.

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:38.000
More rolling.

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:04.000
Mother lost her money.

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:48.500
"You pickpocket."

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:52.750
"Miss, come here!"

00:08:22.750 --> 00:08:28.250
The arrival in the
land of liberty.

00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:15.500
"Good bye"

00:09:33.500 --> 00:09:36.750
Later—hungry and broke.

00:11:17.750 --> 00:11:20.000
"Beans!!!"

00:13:50.000 --> 00:13:52.500
"What's the trouble, waiter?"

00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:55.500
"He was ten cents short."

00:15:07.750 --> 00:15:10.750
"Coffee for the Lady."

00:17:46.250 --> 00:17:49.500
"I am an Artist."

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:28.250
"Bring my check also."

00:19:34.000 --> 00:19:40.000
"I'll engage both of you
now, starting tomorrow."

00:19:44.000 --> 00:19:48.500
"A couple of
dollars on account."

00:20:37.000 --> 00:20:42.250
THE END
